1. g3 e5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. Nf3 e4 5. Nd4 d5 6. cxd5 Qxd5 7. Nc2 Qh5 
8. h3 Na6 9. Nc3 Qg6 10. Ne3 Bc5 11. Qa4 b5 12. Qc2 $1 
    ( 12. Qd1 O-O 13. O-O {was played  in Leko - Svidler, Monte Carlo 
    2005.} )
12. ... Nb4 13. Qb1 $1 Bxe3 $2 
    ( 13. ... O-O $1 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 15. Qxe4 Qxe4 16. Bxe4 f5 17. Bb1 Be6 {
    brings chances for both sides.} )
14. dxe3 Bf5 15. a4 bxa4 16. Nxa4 O-O 17. Bd2 Nfd5 18. Nc5 Rfe8 19. Qc1 a5
20. O-O h5 21. Kh2 Qd6 22. Kg1 h4 23. g4 Bg6 24. Bxb4 Nxb4 25. Rd1 Qe5 $5 
26. Rd4 $1 Rad8 27. Rc4 f5 $2 
    ( 27. ... Rd5 28. Nxe4 Red8 29. f4 Qc7 {offers  more resistance.} )
28. gxf5 Qxf5 29. Rxa5 {Svidler gains a pawn.} 29. ... Rf8 30. Qe1 $5 Rd5 
31. Rxb4 Rxc5 32. Rxc5 Qxc5 33. Bxe4 {A second pawn falls.} 33. ... Qg5+ 
34. Bg2 Bf5 35. Qc3 $5 Bxh3 $1 36. Qxc6 Bxg2 37. Qxg2 Qxg2+ 38. Kxg2 h3+ 
$1 39. Kg3 h2 40. Rh4 $1 {The rook ending is won.} 40. ... Rb8 41. Rxh2 
Rxb2 42. f3 Kf7 43. e4 Kf6 44. e3 Rb3 45. Kf4 g5+ 46. Kg4 Rxe3 47. Rh6+ 
Ke5 48. Rg6 {Svidler equalised the standings in the quarter final.} 1-0

