1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Nxe4 5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 
Nf5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. h3 Bd7 10. Rd1 Be7 11. Nc3 Kc8 12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 
Bxh4 14. Be3 $5 b6 15. Rd2 c5 16. Nd5 Re8 17. Rad1 Bc6 18. Bf4 h6 19. Kg2 
Kb7 20. c4 a5 $6 
    ( 20. ... Bg5 $1 21. Bxg5 hxg5 {equalises.} )
21. Re1 Rad8 22. Bg3 Bxg3 23. Kxg3 f6 24. f4 Re6 25. Rdd1 fxe5 26. Rxe5 $1
Red6 27. f5 a4 $5 28. Kf4 $1 b5 29. b3 a3 $5 {Black could have exchanged.}
30. Ke4 b4 31. h4 R6d7 $5 32. Rd2 Rf7 $5 33. g5 hxg5 34. hxg5 Rh8 35. Kf4 
Rh1 $6 
    ( 35. ... Rh4+ $1 36. Kg3 Rh1 {gains time.} )
36. Rf2 Rg1 37. Ne7 $1 {Black has been restricted.} 37. ... Bh1 $2 
    ( 37. ... Bd7 $1 38. g6 Rf8 {(Szabo)} 39. Rd5 Be8 40. Rxc5 c6 $1 {
    offers a strong  resistance.} )
38. g6 Rf6 39. Rxc5 Rd6 40. Rb5+ Ka6 41. Nd5 Bxd5 42. Rxd5 Rxd5 $5 
    ( 42. ... Rf6 43. Ke3 Re1+ 44. Kd4 {also wins for White.} )
43. cxd5 Kb6 44. f6 $1 gxf6 45. Kf5 Kc5 46. Kxf6 Kxd5 47. g7 c5 48. Rf5+ 
$1 {Caruana won his  fourth game. He triumphed for the second time in 
Dortmund, achieved an elo of 2801 and became number three in the world.} 
1-0

